    {
      "id": "claim_0032d90c9c4c469598eef91acf1d9aa4",
      "statement": "pollForResult on /view/[id] drives the asynchronous run by GETting /api/get-result/{id} with the X-Target-API header every 5 seconds for up to 240 seconds: status OK resolves with the payload, status ACCEPTED keeps polling, any other status throws 'An error occurred while running the pipeline in ardoco: \\n{data.message}' surfacing the backend message, and exhausting the budget throws 'The result is still processing. Please try again later.'",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/app/view/%5Bid%5D/page.tsx#L21-L50",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:78fe7273ecd31616b768d8880ad20378ee329b0c1cca6e35375b3f7399558fc0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bb00843d2c5d42f69de441e83f019aab",
      "statement": "The /view/[id] polling fetch runs with the shared NavigationContext AbortController signal and swallows AbortErrors, so leaving the project — which deletes the OPFS project directory and aborts the controller — ends polling silently; the fetch effect depends on id and apiAddress so changing the configured backend restarts polling, and on status OK the page parses response.traceLinkType with response.result.traceLinks and, when requested and present, response.result.inconsistencies.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/app/view/%5Bid%5D/page.tsx#L90-L118",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8932a3fe0e91cd076aa682b51d8694509e5bb970947123c2c98532c96ff609b6:"
