    {
      "id": "claim_b898393f682a412094f6eae87cad551d",
      "statement": "The two backend callers handle HTTP failures asymmetrically: fetchArdocoApi checks response.ok before parsing the body, while pollForResult parses every /api/get-result response as JSON without checking response.ok, so the middleware's plain-text 400/403 rejections surface on the result page as JSON parse errors rather than as backend messages.",
